Kubernets Auto-Scaling:-
If certain time ,period load increased our define thrashold then our requirement accroding automatic pod created or deleted,
 that is called Auto-Scaling.

 Their have two types:-
1. Horizontal Pod Auto-Scaling (HPA):-
    It is used to scale the number of pods in a deployment or replica set based on CPU utilization or 
    other select metrics.

2. Vertical Pod Auto-Scaling (VPA):-
    It is used automatically adjust the resource requests and limits of pods based on their actual resource usage. 
    It helps to optimize resource allocation and improve performance by ensuring that pods have the necessary
     resources to run efficiently.
Auto-Scaling is an important feature in Kubernetes that allows applications to handle varying workloads 
efficiently by automatically adjusting the number of pods or their resource allocations based on demand. 
This helps to ensure that applications remain responsive and can scale up or down as needed without manual
intervention.

